// boxcxx — <__bits/version_span>
//
// The one feature-test macro [version.syn] gives <span>: P0122R7's span,
// at its C++20 value with P2116R0's deduction guides folded in. Split into a
// leaf for the same [support.limits.general] per-header reason as every other
// version_* file -- see <__bits/version_any> for the full explanation.
//
// It was withheld on three things this document also got partly wrong. The
// claim that span had no crbegin/crend was stale -- both were there. What
// was genuinely missing: the iterator constructors took POINTERS rather than
// an iterator and a sentinel, they were not explicit(extent !=
// dynamic_extent), and the range deduction guide did not exist, so
// `std::span(v)` over a vector could not deduce at all. Ф31e-g closed those.
#ifndef BOXCXX_BITS_VERSION_SPAN
#define BOXCXX_BITS_VERSION_SPAN

#ifndef __cpp_lib_span
#  define __cpp_lib_span 202002L
#endif

#endif // BOXCXX_BITS_VERSION_SPAN
